## Pitfalls summary

- Do not change initial-load results. Garbage at module start still means defaults.
- Do not delete-then-assign before the read is known to be good.
- `""` means absent (reset), kept as `!raw` does today. Do not make it unreadable.
- Arrays now count as unreadable for the object blobs. At initial load they still yield defaults.
- The shape check stays top-level only. A parseable object with a non-object inner entry is still accepted, as today. Do not expand scope.
